  "description": "MOZPAW crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C242 H216 Dy14 N36 O66 P12,5(C3 H7 N1 O1),2(C2 H3 N1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy13 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy14 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 16 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.800-3.968 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.04-113.02°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C261H257Dy14N43O72P12. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
